        <mxCell id="notes-dfs" parent="1" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=#147EBA;fillColor=#E6F2FF;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;fontSize=9;fontColor=#333333;rounded=1;arcSize=5;spacingLeft=5;spacingTop=3;" value="&lt;b&gt;Architecture Notes:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;1. &lt;b&gt;ALB + ASG pattern&lt;/b&gt; replaces standalone EC2 servers.&lt;br&gt;   Host-based routing: mobile.apc.com.pa, tuintelidat.com&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;2. &lt;b&gt;2x FSx for Windows (Single-AZ 1)&lt;/b&gt; - required for DFS-R.&lt;br&gt;   Each in different AZ for resilience (1a + 1b).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;3. &lt;b&gt;2x RDS SQL Server SE&lt;/b&gt;:&lt;br&gt;   - produccion (Multi-AZ, r6i.4xl, 1.7TB)&lt;br&gt;   - procesos (Single-AZ, r6i.2xl, 2.9TB)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;4. EC2 ASG instances boot via &lt;b&gt;Application AMI&lt;/b&gt; (IIS pre-baked).&lt;br&gt;   UserData only does: hostname + domain join + FSx mount.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;5. On-Premise DFS-R replication to dedicated file servers&lt;br&gt;   for DR (10.54.128.x via VPN/Direct Connect)." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="240" width="380" x="1280" y="730" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
